WEBVTT

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.730
Junta, I just remembered 
I have something to do.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.020
Can I drop back?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.490
I forgot an idiot behind us.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.600
You can't! Hakone Academy is approaching!

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.240
We can't lose anyone else!

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.930
I promise, I'll bring him back.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.670
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.760
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.120
I'm telling you not to 
because you can't, Aoyagi!

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:58.780
<i>LINE.09 Sash of Wishes</i>

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.990
You must understand.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:02.760
Makishima-san must've said the 
same thing to Onoda last year.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.130
Dropping back is easy.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:10.370
But bringing someone back with 
you takes twice as much strength.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:11.900
It's a gamble.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:16.700
And we're 1,800 meters up in the mountains.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.370
You're a sprinter. You can't do it.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.490
Letting you go back to save him now

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.580
would be the same as losing two 
members of our six-man team.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:30.670
We'll be stronger with all six of us.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.290
I'm bringing him back.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:40.970
Aoyagi, I can give you about seven more 
reasons why your choice is reckless.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.360
Wanna hear them?

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.730
No, I'm good.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.640
You're going, then?

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.420
I'm going.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.110
Then this is goodbye.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.590
A-Aoyagi-san...

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.340
You're going to rescue Kaburagi-kun 
and come back, right?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.090
There are no certainties in road racing.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.910
Junta's right. This is reckless.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.690
You must always be prepared 
for your plans to fail.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.230
We're third-years. This is our last race.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.760
If you can't make it back, this will 
be the last time we ride together.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:27.510
<b>Certain</b>

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:26.730
Thanks for riding with me these 
last three years, Hajime.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.980
Our two-man team was the greatest.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.860
Yeah, Junta.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.070
I made it this far because of you.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.950
<i>Our two-man team...</i>

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:47.990
<i>...is dissolved!</i>

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.380
Aoyagi-san!

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.930
Don't look back, Onoda.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.710
Ride with Junta and reach the 
front before Hakone Academy.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.210
Support Imaizumi and Naruko as best you can.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:58.880
Yes, sir!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.590
That's your job!

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.090
Yes!

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:06.300
Junta, tell me one last thing.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:11.300
Those seven more reasons my choice 
is reckless... Is there an eighth?

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.650
What? The eighth?

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.440
There's...

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.820
There is one.

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.820
It's a tiny shred of hope!

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:27.740
Then pray the eighth
 turns out to be true, Junta!

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.980
Aoyagi-san's been swallowed 
by Hakone Academy!

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.660
I know! Face forward!

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.790
We'll catch them first! Raise the pace!

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.670
Yes, sir!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.670
Sohoku's second rider has fallen.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.590
Damn it! I feel weak.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.560
Why?

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.990
<i>My limbs are heavy.</i>

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.110
<i>My pedals are heavy.</i>

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.810
<i>They've never felt this heavy before.</i>

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:05.360
<i>Come on. Come on, strength!</i>

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.370
I'm Fukuoka Zosei's Obori!

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:13.240
You were showing off during yesterday's 
sprint, Sohoku's Kaburagi!

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.120
And now you're mine!

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:16.790
You can't catch me!

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:17.830
I will!

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.820
Kaburagi probably won't be able to 
group up with Aoyagi right away.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:27.630
What?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.320
He's too far behind.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:33.900
He may be trying to rescue him,
 but at the very least,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.520
Kaburagi will have to reach Aoyagi on his own.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.150
If his spirit is broken, and he's 
stopped moving, they'll never meet up.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.850
B-But...

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:47.990
He'll be fine if someone's 
there to give him a push.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.420
But that won't happen.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:56.290
Before we started, nobody noticed
 that he wasn't feeling well.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.410
<i>What am I going to do?</i>

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.830
<i>Is this the end already?</i>

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.470
Don't stop, Kaburagi!

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.630
Huh?

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.640
Keep moving forward!

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.360
Put your feet on the pedals.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.060
The race isn't over yet.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.850
Koga-san?

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.270
Huh? What?

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.610
What are you doing here?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:24.890
Did you warp here?

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.110
Cast a magic spell?

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.140
There's no time to talk.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.670
Focus on the race.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:31.240
Put your feet on the pedals.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.450
Move forward, Kaburagi!

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.740
Don't stop!

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:39.160
You must always move forward in a road race.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:42.320
Standing still is the same as forfeiting.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.300
If you abandon the Inter-High now...

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.800
I'll make sure you pay for it!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.310
<i>Crap. He's serious.</i>

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:53.540
<i>He wholeheartedly means 
everything he's saying.</i>

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.720
<i>It has weight.</i>

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.230
<i>I can feel it all the way to my fingertips.</i>

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.110
<i>But...</i>

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:07.650
Move!

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.360
Yes, sir!

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:12.490
No matter what happens,
 keep moving forward, Kaburagi!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:13.370
Yes!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:16.240
Koga-san, the van is leaving soon.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:18.870
Go on without me.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.210
Huh?

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.370
I'll stay here.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.170
What? Why do you want us 
to leave without you?

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.380
There's something bothering me.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.930
You take command of the feed zone, Sugimoto.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.500
What? Wait a minute.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:34.870
What do you...

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:37.740
<i>"I've been worried about 
Kaburagi since this morning."</i>

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.480
<i>It'd be a disaster if I said that, 
and it turned out to be true.</i>

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:42.910
You're staying?

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:45.690
I imagined the worst case scenario.

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:48.980
For the team, huh?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.950
If you stay now, you won't 
make it to the feed zone.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.080
Sorry for being stubborn.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:05.530
<i>Let this hike have been a 
waste of time, Kaburagi.</i>

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.020
<i>But...</i>

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.340
If you can't move...

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:16.680
Then I'll push you!

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.370
A short push is fine,

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.250
but a long push from anyone other than 
another rider is against the rules.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.060
I'll be penalized.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:26.530
Then I'll push little by little.

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:28.070
That shouldn't be a problem.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:33.400
Supporting you as best we can is our job!

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.110
<i>Koga-san...</i>

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.590
<i>Sohoku still has a chance.</i>

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.100
Sorry, Koga-san! Thank you!

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:47.500
<i>So you can say "thank you," Kaburagi.</i>

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.880
<i>The old me thought it was natural.</i>

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:54.020
<i>That Teshima and Aoyagi 
were assigned to support us</i>

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:56.090
<i>because they didn't work hard enough.</i>

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.160
<i>That's not how it is.</i>

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:01.170
<i>We're able to move forward 
because we all support each other.</i>

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:05.110
Believe that you'll rejoin the team!

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:05.600
Yes, sir!

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:09.610
Imagine yourself returning 
to form as you ride!

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:10.820
Yes, sir!

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:16.550
Keep racing and grow with 
everything you've got!

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:17.530
I know you can do it!

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:20.410
You have the most potential!

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:21.660
Huh?

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.420
Yes, sir!

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:29.130
Imagine, imagine, imagine!

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.800
Imagine your recovery!

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:35.340
Slow riders, please move to the left!

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:36.970
Huh?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.670
The pack is coming through!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.270
<i>The pack...</i>

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:52.390
The pack... passed us.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.190
In an instant...

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.280
<i>Even the pack passed him.</i>

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.120
<i>Someone stopped!</i>

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:12.130
Go, Kaburagi! You can still make it!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.380
Your teammate is waiting for you!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.260
Tie your sash of wishes to his!

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.050
Huh?

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.600
<i>He's right. I can see him.</i>

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:21.890
<i>He's wearing a Sohoku jersey!</i>

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:27.540
Go, Kaburagi!

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.020
Connect that thread of hope!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.860
Koga-san, thank you!

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.750
<i>Who could have imagined it?</i>

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:48.250
<i>That as hands reached out to catch falling 
drops of hope, some would fall through...</i>

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:53.210
<i>And another hand would 
reach out to catch them.</i>

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:59.680
<i>Thank you for waiting for me 
when I'm in such bad shape.</i>

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.870
<i>Now I might be able to return to the team.</i>

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:05.430
<i>My Inter-High...</i>

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.680
<i>...isn't over yet!</i>

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.810
<i>Who is it? Teshima-san?</i>

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:11.600
<i>Onoda-san?</i>

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:15.980
Huh?

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.360
Aoyagi-san?

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.030
That's right.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.890
Seriously?

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:25.910
Aoyagi-san...

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:33.140
You were riding in front of us during 
the chase, so we could reach the front.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.540
But you're...

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:36.170
That's right.

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:39.990
You're a third-year.
 This is your last Inter-high.

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:43.930
But you're here now, which means...

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.180
That's right.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.520
You fell behind the team, too?

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:56.190
Did you fall behind the team, too?

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:57.440
No!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.690
Can't you tell from the situation?

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.410
I was waiting for you!

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:03.100
The situation?

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:06.120
Wait. Why do you look like 
you feel sorry for me?

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.570
Oh, no.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.370
I understand. I get it.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:14.380
You don't want to admit that 
you fell behind the team.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.420
You're desperately trying to save face.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.980
<i>Does he really not get it?</i>

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:19.370
<i>He doesn't get it.</i>

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:23.470
I was hoping you were 
Onoda-san or Teshima-san.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.550
<i>Who says that to someone's face?</i>

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.930
It doesn't matter. Follow me.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.460
<i>Did Koga push him?</i>

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:37.350
<i>You're the only one on 
Sohoku who saw this coming.</i>

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:44.220
<i>You're the greatest support 
Sohoku has ever had, Kimitaka.</i>

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:45.280
Let's go, Kaburagi!

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.620
We're going to reach the 
team at the front together!

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:50.150
Seriously?

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:52.170
You and me?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.180
That's right.

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:54.370
It'll be hard, but we'll do it.

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:58.250
So follow me. Don't fall behind.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:01.920
No complaining.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.300
Yes, sir!

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.550
<i>What's with this intensity?</i>

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:11.500
Supersonic Oxygen Muscle Climb!

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:16.980
<i>He's falling behind.</i>

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.270
<i>He still doesn't feel well?</i>

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:23.440
<i>If I raise my pace, 
Kaburagi will fall behind.</i>

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.330
<i>He can't do what should be easy for him.</i>

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.070
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:32.910
You're knitting your brows.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.080
You look pained, Aoyagi.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:41.390
You called it your "Muscle Climb," 
but your pace has fallen so quickly.

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:42.800
<i>Whose fault is that?</i>

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.340
Then I don't have a choice, Aoyagi!

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:51.350
<i>Wh-What?</i>

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:55.310
See that? Sohoku's already 
lost two of their riders.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.950
They were doing so well yesterday.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.450
Maybe they're just not that good this year.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:02.760
Enough, Kawamoto, Okutani.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:03.730
Yamagiwa-san...

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:07.820
#4 is trying to bring their
 out-of-form #6 back to the team.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:10.050
What? From back there?

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:11.920
But that's impossible.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.910
Maybe.

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:18.510
But last year they won from #170.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.960
I think...

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:27.470
Sohoku might be strongest 
when they're facing adversity.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.970
I don't have a choice!

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.550
What are you doing, Kaburagi?

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.420
Why are you pulling?

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.060
Fall back! I'll pull!

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:39.790
Look at you showing off and pushing yourself.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:41.200
Fine, then.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:43.420
I'll pull, too!

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.900
Hey, listen!

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.050
I'm fine.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:51.170
I feel a little better now.

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:53.910
Koga-san gave me power.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.710
"Grow."

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:59.170
"You have great potential."

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:03.130
You should quit showing off
 and rest behind me, Aoyagi.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.290
<i>That's Aoyagi-</i>san<i> to you!</i>

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:10.380
<i>I'll see how he does and
 move up if he drops his pace.</i>

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:14.600
<i>Kaburagi's still pulling.</i>

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.890
<i>Well, well. He's still pulling.</i>

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:23.770
You're a lot of trouble, Aoyagi.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.520
<i>Huh? He's still pulling?</i>

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.030
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:34.410
<i>He's faster when he's pulling 
than when he's being pulled.</i>

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:39.280
Are you keeping up, Aoyagi?

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:40.000
Yeah.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:43.830
<i>How is this happening? But it's true.</i>

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.640
I'm a little surprised, though.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:49.620
By what? The view?

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:55.340
<i>I've never heard of the one being 
rescued pulling for his rescuer.</i>

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.220
The view is nice.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.770
<i>Half of road racing is mental.</i>

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.870
<i>If your spirit is broken, it's over.</i>

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.390
<i>But if you have a goal, you can keep moving.</i>

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:13.690
<i>He's doing his best to 
move forward to help me.</i>

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.490
<i>He's still confused, though.</i>

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:19.610
Aoyagi, how are you feeling?

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:22.460
Like I've been saying, I feel great.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.540
There you go again.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.210
You can be honest with me.

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:30.630
<i>In any case, he isn't just an idiot.</i>

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.340
<i>He's a special idiot!</i>

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:37.530
Breathe with me!

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:40.290
Ready and...

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:44.890
<i>This just might be...</i>

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:50.400
But isn't one of Sohoku's 
riders out of sorts?

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:53.820
That's right. The unexpected doesn't happen.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.910
If they're able to catch up to the pack,

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:00.850
it'll be in a style that defies common sense.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.250
Someone's coming up from behind!

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.390
It's the two Sohoku riders!

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.380
Th-The redhead is in front!

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.730
Isn't it the other way around?

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:15.130
Didn't #4 go to save him?

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:19.860
I see them!

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:23.270
It's the pack that passed us earlier!

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.370
We caught up to them!

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.440
<i>He's impressive.</i>

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:36.200
<i>Just by imagining he was saving me,
 he pulled me until we could see the pack.</i>

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:38.110
We're almost there!

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:41.950
Once we catch up and enter the pack, 
you'll be able to rest, Aoyagi!

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:43.750
<i>Yeah, you will.</i>

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.160
<i>Your speech has gotten really casual.</i>

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:50.170
<i>Let us reach them!</i>

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:53.170
Docking!

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:56.130
Sohoku returned to the pack!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.410
But they were stopped earlier! Seriously?

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:00.220
Who are those guys?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.730
We joined the pack...

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:22.030
Did you feel exhausted for a second?

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:24.510
What? N-No.

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:28.140
I was just looking at a 
rare bug on the ground.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.380
What kind of bug?

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:36.260
Huh? Uh, kinda like a rhinoceros beetle or a
 stag beetle. It's called a rhinostag beetle.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:40.020
<i>So he barely made it through the first stage.</i>

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:43.390
<i>I'd like to catch up to the team soon,</i>

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:45.940
<i>but he's still not in top shape.</i>

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:49.130
<i>It'll be easier for him in the pack, 
where there's less air resistance.</i>

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:51.110
<i>I'll let him rest for a while.</i>

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.750
Anyway, you should get some rest, Aoyagi.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.360
Yeah, you should.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.150
<i>But...</i>

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.740
Let's move up, Kaburagi!

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:02.660
Huh?

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:08.960
I get it. We're counting our opponents.

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:15.230
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight...

00:19:11.570 --> 00:19:13.330
<i>I don't see them.</i>

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.230
<i>Have they already left?</i>

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:16.340
Huh?

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:20.340
Kyoto Fushimi's not in the pack.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:24.180
<i>His ability to sniff out his 
opponents is first rate.</i>

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:28.000
This isn't good.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.130
Did I notice first?

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:31.880
That doesn't matter.

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:33.510
So you agree it was me, then?

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:37.230
They have #116 this year, too.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:41.180
If they meet up with Midousuji...

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.770
M-Muscles!

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:47.700
Sohoku will be at a massive disadvantage!

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.080
The other strong teams are missing, too.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:54.470
Then we don't have time to rest, Aoyagi!

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:56.790
I could say the same thing to you.

00:19:57.610 --> 00:20:01.490
We're ditching this pack, Aoyagi!

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.260
Sohoku's pulling ahead!

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.980
Did you see a rare bug?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:20.400
<i>He understands the situation, 
but his body won't move.</i>

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:23.660
<i>He must be frustrated.</i>

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:28.370
<i>Did you see this coming too, Junta?</i>

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.950
What? They won't be able to escape the pack?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.750
Yeah, even if they do make it to the pack.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:38.630
Leaving the pack is fairly difficult.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:43.090
That's reason four of seven 
that his choice was reckless.

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:46.300
Is it really impossible?

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:50.810
It's a different story if he's 
made special preparations.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.090
Special preparations?

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:59.230
Kaburagi, do you want to leave 
the pack, no matter what?

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.900
Of course, damn it.

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:04.530
What if there was a way?

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:05.070
Huh?

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.140
Do you have something?

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:11.690
I wasn't expecting to use this here.

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:13.680
I'll do anything.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:14.710
Tell me!

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.260
It's this.

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:23.670
G-God's stationery?

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:25.570
I knew God would come through.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:27.560
He's written a hint on it.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:31.810
The princess...?

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:34.060
Those are the lyrics to a certain song.

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:37.130
"You are the princess"?

00:23:15.860 --> 00:23:18.700
Hikki the Third, grow up big and strong!

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:19.620
Hey.

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:21.720
Huh?

00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:23.410
What are you doing?

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:25.370
Wait!

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:30.770
Hey! What was that for?

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:32.580
What about my Hikki-san?

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:33.910
You idiot!

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:36.450
Is he still a kid?

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT LINE  #16, Shinkai Yuto</i>

